              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 70,
                "start": 70
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Messenger, compelling employees to subsidize unions is akin to protection money and is not a compelling governmental interest that can justify infringing First Amendment rights."
        },
